# Global-over-link-local IPv4 preference for BIND_IP interface resolution.
#
# Product reason: the AoIP addressing ladder (static/DHCP -> link-local
# via the netifd 'zcip' proto, busybox RFC 3927) keeps the Dante segment
# addressable even standalone on a bare switch — at the price of the
# bound device carrying BOTH a global (DHCP/static) and a 169.254/16
# address in the combined single-port topology. The old scan took the
# first address found, which is arbitrary in that regime; Dante peers on
# a managed network must reach the advertised address, so the first
# GLOBAL IPv4 wins, with link-local as the standalone fallback.
#
# Upstream-rev: 75d9198 + 0001 + 0002 + 0003. Generated with git diff
# from the stacked tree; `cargo test -p inferno_aoip` covers the
# preference (global-first both orders, link-local-only fallback, empty).
